WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.010
A Friday in May.

2
00:00:02.060 --> 00:00:07.130
Malware called WannaCry locks files on
computers across the world and demands

3
00:00:07.180 --> 00:00:08.330
a ransom.

4
00:00:08.380 --> 00:00:10.990
In England, it hits the NHS.

5
00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:13.870
Hundreds of NHS
organisations are affected,

6
00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:16.590
and thousands of
appointments are cancelled.

7
00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:17.990
But rewind to March.

8
00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:23.370
NHS Digital had already sent critical
alerts telling organisations to patch

9
00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:24.690
their systems.

10
00:00:24.740 --> 00:00:29.630
So if the fix already existed,
why did WannaCry still get in?

11
00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:34.830
In this mission, you'll find out what
malware is and how it gets onto a computer.

12
00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:38.610
You'll see what a vulnerability
is, and how a patch fixes it.

13
00:00:38.660 --> 00:00:42.670
And you'll see how anti-malware
hunts for known malware.

14
00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:47.440
Your mission: explain why
WannaCry still hit the NHS in May.
